# Banking Transactions API — sample requests
# Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (click "Send Request" above each block),
# or read them as a reference for curl. Server must be running on http://localhost:8000.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

### Create a transaction (201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "ACC-12345",
  "toAccount": "ACC-67890",
  "amount": 100.50,
  "currency": "USD",
  "type": "transfer"
}

### Create a deposit
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "ACC-BANK01",
  "toAccount": "ACC-12345",
  "amount": 500.00,
  "currency": "USD",
  "type": "deposit"
}

### Validation failure (400) — negative amount + bad currency
POST {{baseUrl}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "ACC-12345",
  "toAccount": "ACC-67890",
  "amount": -10,
  "currency": "ZZZ",
  "type": "transfer"
}

### List all transactions
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions

### Filter by account
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?accountId=ACC-12345

### Filter by type
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?type=transfer

### Filter by date range + account (combined)
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions?accountId=ACC-12345&from=2024-01-01&to=2099-12-31

### Get a transaction by id (replace with a real id from a create response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/REPLACE_WITH_ID

### Account balance
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/ACC-12345/balance

### Account summary (Task 4 - Option A)
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/ACC-12345/summary

### Export transactions as CSV (Task 4 - Option C)
GET {{baseUrl}}/transactions/export?format=csv
